# Left unset on purpose: the frontend calls its own "/api" and Vercel proxies
# it server-side to the backend (see vercel.json) rather than the browser
# calling the backend's URL directly. That's what keeps the auth cookie
# first-party — automated-emailer-frontend.vercel.app and
# automated-emailer-backend.vercel.app are different *sites* (both are
# subdomains of the public suffix vercel.app), so a cookie set by a direct
# cross-site fetch to the backend gets treated as third-party and blocked by
# the browser regardless of correct SameSite=None/Secure/CORS config.
#
# If you ever host the frontend somewhere without server-side proxying
# (or on a real custom domain where frontend/backend are true subdomains of
# one site), set this to the backend's full URL instead:
# VITE_API_URL=https://your-backend.example.com/api
